1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Roomwise helps Virginia Tech students understand housing before choosing a lease.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Search forty-four priced properties, with one card per place. Floor plans, price ranges and original billing labels stay together.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The housing guide adds broader neighborhood context, with forty-seven community and neighborhood references.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Set your budget, household size, bedroom needs and travel preferences. These inputs stay connected across the workflow.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Each plan separates rent, fees and deposits. Open the evidence to inspect source dates, original disclosures and disagreements.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Missing facts become a written-quote request. Copy it to confirm exact fees, dates and availability. Nothing is sent automatically.

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Investigate nearby essentials, change the search radius in miles, and review mapped grocery stores and directions links.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Compare shortlisted plans side by side. Monthly rent and installments retain their labels; roommate splits remain planning scenarios.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Here is the locally fine-tuned Gemma four assistant responding to a real question. The interface identifies the actual model and its limitations. Application code owns the calculations; generated guidance still needs verification.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Attach questions to a property and save a decision brief, freezing the prices, sources and inputs behind your comparison.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
DormToDoor turns unresolved facts into a practical, editable before-you-sign checklist.

12
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Roomwise: know the trade-offs, and what to verify next.
